---
import Doodle from "./Doodle.astro";
import Layout from "./Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="jwstn.dev — JW's sketchbook"
  description="Full-stack developer in Cologne, penciling web apps on graph paper — TanStack concepts, Effect experiments and taped-in reference prints."
>
  <article class="sk-home">
    <!-- sheet 01: the concept hero -->
    <section class="sk-hero sk-woobble" aria-labelledby="sk-hero-title">
      <p class="sk-margin-note" aria-hidden="true">hero_v4_FINAL_final — don't erase!</p>

      <p class="sk-kicker">sheet 01 · concept · jwstn.dev · cologne, de</p>
      <h1 class="sk-hero-title" id="sk-hero-title">
        Hey — <span class="sk-circled">I'm JW<Doodle name="circle" draw class="sk-circle" /></span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="sk-hero-sub">full-stack developer. i sketch web apps in pencil before i commit them to code.</p>

      <div class="sk-hero-bio sk-ruled">
        <p>
          most days i'm deep in
          <a href="https://tanstack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TanStack</a> — it hands
          me most of what a web app needs, server actions and middleware included. which is exactly why
          <a href="https://hono.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hono</a> and
          <a href="https://elysiajs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Elysia</a> are still
          sitting in the "someday" margin of this sheet. the rabbit hole i
          <em>did</em> go down is <a href="https://effect.website/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Effect</a> —
          amazing fun so far, and a genuinely new way to think about programs.
          <span class="sk-rednote">keep this bit<Doodle name="star" class="sk-rednote-star" /></span>
        </p>
        <p class="sk-hand">
          ps — the camera i brought home from japan in 2026 hasn't left my bag since. the whole roll is
          taped up in the <a href="/gallery">reference prints</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="sk-dim sk-hero-dim">100% HAND-DRAWN · NO PIXELS HARMED</p>
    </section>

    <!-- three wireframe boxes pointing at the rest of the site -->
    <section aria-labelledby="sk-board-title">
      <h2 class="sk-section-title" id="sk-board-title">
        on the drawing board
        <Doodle name="underline" draw class="sk-doodle-underline" />
      </h2>
      <ul class="sk-home-cards">
        <li>
          <div class="sk-card sk-woobble">
            <p class="sk-fig">fig. 1 — the work</p>
            <h3><a href="/projects">Concept sheets</a></h3>
            <p>
              four sheets so far: a vinyl collection forum, a terminal spotify client, an app for learning
              sign language, and one very personal todo list.
            </p>
            <a class="sk-cardlink" href="/projects">open the sheets</a>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="sk-card sk-woobble">
            <p class="sk-fig">fig. 2 — the pin board</p>
            <div class="sk-mini" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="sk-mini-bar"></span>
              <span class="sk-mini-bar short"></span>
              <p class="sk-mini-label">TBD</p>
            </div>
            <h3><a href="/blog">Notes</a></h3>
            <p>
              a fresh sheet, nothing pinned to it yet. the first note is somewhere between a rough sketch
              and a napkin.
            </p>
            <a class="sk-cardlink" href="/blog">look at the empty board</a>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="sk-card sk-woobble">
            <p class="sk-fig">fig. 3 — the camera roll</p>
            <div class="sk-mini-print" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 96 72" fill="none" stroke="#3a3f47" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <circle cx="24" cy="16" r="7.5"></circle>
                <path d="M4 60 C 18 46, 32 50, 44 58 C 56 48, 72 40, 92 58"></path>
                <path d="M4 60 L 92 60" stroke-width="1.6" opacity="0.6"></path>
                <path d="M14 34 l4 -6 4 6 M30 32 l3 -5 3 5" opacity="0.5"></path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3><a href="/gallery">Reference prints</a></h3>
            <p>
              cologne walks, spring blossoms, and a japan 2026 roll — printed and taped in as the film
              comes back.
            </p>
            <a class="sk-cardlink" href="/gallery">flip through the prints</a>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
